# Focused equivalence for the $pmux techmap rule.
#
#   gold = the probe's $pmux cell rewritten to $mux cells by Yosys `pmuxtree`
#          (the tool's own definition of the cell, not ours)
#   gate = the probe after `techmap -map sky130_map.v`, with the mux2_1 cells
#          flattened to their behavioural model
#
# Equivalence is per module, so a mismatch in one probe cannot be averaged away.
# Run from the repository root: yosys -s asic/synthesis/techmap/equiv_pmux.ys
#
# Order matters: the cell model is read AFTER techmap, otherwise the map file
# also expands the model's own $not/$and/$or cells and the gate side is left
# with undefined sky130 cells.

read_rtlil asic/synthesis/techmap/pmux_probe.il
techmap -map build/asic_evidence/sky130_map.v
opt -fast
read_verilog asic/synthesis/techmap/pmux_cell_model.v
flatten pmux_s1_w8 pmux_s3_w8 pmux_s1_w1
opt -fast
rename pmux_s1_w8 gate_s1_w8
rename pmux_s3_w8 gate_s3_w8
rename pmux_s1_w1 gate_s1_w1
design -stash gate

read_rtlil asic/synthesis/techmap/pmux_probe.il
pmuxtree
opt -fast
rename pmux_s1_w8 gold_s1_w8
rename pmux_s3_w8 gold_s3_w8
rename pmux_s1_w1 gold_s1_w1
design -stash gold

# ---- WIDTH 8, S_WIDTH 1 (the case that was broken) ------------------------
design -copy-from gate -as gate_s1_w8 gate_s1_w8
design -copy-from gold -as gold_s1_w8 gold_s1_w8
equiv_make gate_s1_w8 gold_s1_w8 equiv_s1_w8
hierarchy -top equiv_s1_w8
equiv_simple
equiv_status -assert

# ---- WIDTH 8, S_WIDTH 3: measured, deliberately not asserted -------------
# Measured on 2026-11-18: the mapper chain and Yosys `pmuxtree` disagree when
# more than one select bit is set, because they pick different priorities. The
# $pmux contract is one-hot, so both are legal and neither is the reference off
# contract. Asserting it here would fail for a reason that is not a defect.
# One-hot behaviour of this probe is covered exhaustively by tb_pmux_map.v
# (every select value with all 256 values of A and B).

# ---- WIDTH 1, S_WIDTH 1 ---------------------------------------------------
design -copy-from gate -as gate_s1_w1 gate_s1_w1
design -copy-from gold -as gold_s1_w1 gold_s1_w1
equiv_make gate_s1_w1 gold_s1_w1 equiv_s1_w1
hierarchy -top equiv_s1_w1
equiv_simple
equiv_status -assert
